    "seoTitle": "",
    "seoDescription": "",
    "originalPath": "/doors-2/how-to-measure-window-glass-for-a-replacement-without-replacing-the-whole-frame",
    "content": "<p>Replacing a broken or foggy window pane doesn't mean you need to tear out the whole window and spend a small fortune on a full unit replacement. If your frame is still sturdy, opting for a <b>glass-only replacement</b> (whether for a picture window or double-hung sash) saves serious money and time.</p><p>The secret to a seamless DIY fix comes down to getting your tape measure out and taking accurate dimensions. Here is how to measure your window glass like a pro before ordering your replacement pane.</p><h3>Step-by-Step Measuring Instructions</h3><p><b>1. </b><b>Measure the Width</b> Hold your tape measure horizontally and record the distance between the inner edges of the vinyl or wood stops that secure the glass inside the frame.</p><p><b>2. </b><b>Measure the Height</b> Run your tape measure vertically between the inner edges of the vinyl or wood stops holding the glass in place.</p><p><img src=\"/wp-media/uploads/2026/09/GlassMeasureGuide-551x600.png\" alt=\"Glass Measuring Guide\" /></p><h3>Pro-Tips to Avoid Pricey Mistakes</h3><ul><li><p><b>Measure where the glass sits:</b> Always focus on the edge-to-edge area inside the frame where the glass actually rests.</p></li><li><p><b>Ignore the outer trim:</b><b>Do NOT</b> measure the exterior window frame or decorative trim surrounding the window. Including the trim will result in ordering a pane that is far too large to fit into your sash.</p></li></ul><p><b>Ready to get your window back in top shape?</b> Grab your measurements and contact us today to order your custom-cut replacement glass!</p>"
