    "seoDescription": "Edmonds, WA home transformation by Sound View! We installed energy-efficient Milgard windows and doors. See our project showcase!",
    "originalPath": "/doors-2/project-showcase-a-full-home-window-door-transformation-in-edmonds-wa",
    "content": "<p>We recently wrapped up an exciting and comprehensive window and door replacement project for a homeowner in the Edmonds, WA area! This extensive remodel involved replacing nearly two dozen existing units across two floors, significantly boosting the home's energy efficiency, curb appeal, and functionality.</p><h3>The Scope of Work</h3><p>The project involved a full tear-out and replacement of 23 units.. The replacement units were chosen from Milgard's popular vinyl product lines, ensuring durability and high performance:</p><p><b>Milgard V300 Trinsic Vinyl:</b> Used for all sliding windows and sliding patio doors.. These provide a clean, contemporary look with excellent operability3</p><p><b>Milgard V250 Style Line Vinyl:</b> Selected for the picture windows.. This series offers slim frames that maximize the viewable glass area.</p><h3>Key Product Highlights</h3><p>The new windows and doors feature key upgrades designed to improve the home's comfort and energy savings:</p><p><b>Color Consistency:</b> All units, both interior and exterior, were specified in <b>White</b> for a cohesive and bright look against the home’s exterior siding.</p><p><b>Energy-Efficient Glass:</b> Most units were outfitted with <b>SuncoatMax Clear with LowE</b> or <b>Suncoat Clear with LowE</b> glass.. Low-E coatings are essential for managing solar heat gain and improving insulation, which is crucial for Seattle-area weather8.</p><p><b>Specialty Glass:</b> For one of the Front Bedroom windows, we installed a <b>Suncoat Obscure with LowE</b> glass with a frosted stain etched finish.. This provides privacy without sacrificing natural light.</p><p><b>Sliding Doors:</b> We installed three new sliding patio doors in the Den, Dining Room, and another area, all featuring White hardware and upgraded keyed screen surrounds for security and convenience.</p><h3>Installation Details</h3><p>Our installation process was meticulous to ensure a clean finish and proper weatherproofing:</p><p><b>Full Frame Installation:</b> We utilized a nailing flange installation method for a secure and watertight seal</p><p><b>Exterior Trim:</b> To ensure a clean, professional transition, we applied <b>5/4 x 2 primed cedar exterior trim</b> around all the new units. This material is primed and ready for the homeowner to paint to match their exterior color perfectly.</p><p><b>Window Remodeling:</b> We even managed a major change in the Master Bedroom by dropping the sill a full 12 inches to accommodate a new $96^{\\prime\\prime} \\times 48^{\\prime\\prime}$ horizontal sliding window</p>"
